  [E#link("F_p")[2] \= Z/2, generated by T₀ \= (0, 0) in Montgomery
  form],
  [exactly one translation acts on the x-line: u ↦ 1/u. This is the only
  pairwise symmetry available to summation polynomials over F\_p.],
  [rational points of order 4 and 8 exist (u \= ±1 have order 4)],
  [translation by them is not a function of x. Any coordinate on which
  T₄ acts is invariant under 2T₄ \= T₀, so it lives on E/⟨T₀⟩, where T₄
  has become a 2-torsion point: the same symmetry on an isogenous curve,
  not a new one
  (`research/notes/index-calculus/RESEARCH_EXOTIC_COORDINATES.md`
