  [every point has a cofactor coset c ∈ Z/8. A sum of two base points
  lands in the subgroup iff their cosets cancel. This is the quantity
  every algebraic-track gain in this atlas comes from (§5).],
)
]

== 2. Coordinates and curve models
<coordinates-and-curve-models>
Every separable degree-2 coordinate f: E → P¹ is the quotient by an
involution P ↦ T′ − P; conjugating by a translation moves T′ to O, so f
\= N(x(P + S)) for a Möbius map N ∈ PGL₂ and a point S
(`src/cryptanalysis/coordinate_search.rs`, checked numerically there). A
factor base "f(P) in an interval" is therefore a Möbius frame of x,
translated by S. The translation shifts every log by log S; on the
algebraic track that changes the coset of every pair sum by 2·c(S) and
nothing else.

