Ideas considered and not pursued, with the reason:

- #strong[Two towers with complementary cosets] (cross pairs only):
  bounded by 1/0.75 ≈ 1.33× over the selected single tower, below the
  measurement noise of a 16-target session.
- #strong[Montgomery-form S₃ per-target cost]: coefficient size is
  irrelevant mod p and the term structure is identical; the only
  measured form-dependence (Edwards, G \= 0) vanishes at the cells that
  matter.
- #strong[Edwards-x bases]: a translate by an order-4 point; identical
  to a frame plus lifts.
- #strong[y-coordinate or higher-degree coordinates]: degree penalty, as
  T2.
- #strong[Working on E/⟨T₈⟩ or another isogenous curve]: the discrete
  logarithm is isogeny-invariant and the isogenous curve has its own
  cofactor cosets; nothing is gained beyond moving the frame.
- #strong[Weil restriction to F\_{p²}]: the target and base stay in
  E(F\_p); no new symmetry appears.
- #strong[Coset-pure filtering]: loses to selection (§5).
- #strong[Multi-target amortisation] (precompute base logs once): a
  reporting convention (`ecbench amortize`), not a new method; it does
  not change the per-relation F4 cost that dominates.

